³1version³21³2ts³21098878608³2ip³2205.231.31.86³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= Freedom Moneys =

[Note: replace monies in title too. the subj is enough without 'monies'.]

Freedom moneys are moneys that advance or at least don't impair the concept of freedom. In general the less the govt has to do with controlling a money the freer that money is, and the more of a freedom money it is.

The finest freedom money is of course gold, followed very closely by silver. But, new freedom moneys or rather currencies are appearing:

Net engendered currencies or eMetals like eGold, etc.

Generally, many already understand some of the advantages of this. Ultimately, that needs to be addressed, but for now, I want to tighten the commerce by tracking usages and costs. As in--

#Cost to keep gold there.
#Convenience to get value in there.
#Convenience to get gold in there.
#Cost to transfer value out.
#Cost to transfer gold out.
#Cost to cash out.
#Convenience to cash out.
#Anonymity.
#Rated trust of company.

Maybe a table of these and the companies offering will do for a bit. There are already a number of companies competing in this market, but all is still developing. The starting point has unfortunately been business models that have developed or been distorted by many years of government interference. It will take some time to recover.

My opinion here concerns particularly the privacy or anonymity involved in the services and the fee schedules. The forerunner in this is Digital Money Trust (DMT) of [http://orlingrabbe.com Orlin Grabbe]. DMT offers total anonymity and DMT charges 1/10 of 1% for internal transfers (where 1% is seen as 'normal'). I would expect all computer-driven transfer fees to approach zero.

Note that often it 'costs' 1% p.a. to just hold the gold. So after forty years, you retire with 60% of what you saved. Ten pounds of gold is a 'small' bar or 120 one-ounce coins and is currently worth about $50,000. Perhaps a safe is in order.

- - -

<b>Gold, Silver, Platinum, Palladium, and Rhodium Bullions</b>

They all all working their way into the commodity money mix. As of 02 Oct '04:

||Metal||$/oz||
||Gold||$420||
||Silver||$6.92||
||Platinum||$872||
||Palladium||$236||
||Rhodium||$1300||

E-gold Ltd, a Nevis corporation, 100% backed at all times by gold bullion in allocated storage... claims registered trademark to e-gold, e-metal, e-silver, e-platinum, and e-palladium, afaik. Interesting IP bandwagen.

Then, there's Digital Money Trust (DMT) of [http://orlingrabbe.com Orlin Grabbe] for anonymous security.

- - -

From kbarrett's post from TCF:

E-gold is a US based entity .... but you can trade e-gold for other anonymous metal based currencies, like pecunix.

[https://www.1mdc.com/ If you move your gold into 1mdc, it will become anonymous.]

You can then trade it out from there using [http://open2exchange.com/buy.sell.. Open2Exchange].

If you need help funding, these folks can help: [http://www.goldnow.st/Page.aspx GoldNow]

And finally, I would suggest checking any service out [http://www.gdcaonline.org/ here first.] Only use Silver or better rated members.

----

040921, JunkerIn. Added.

Here: E-gold, Gold Now, 1MDC

- - -

<b>E-gold - http://e-gold.com/</b>


<i>Create an account.</i>

The short explanation-

#Account Name ("ABC Widgets Inc")
#User Name ("Joe Hampton", "Dr. N.")
#Point of Contact  (name and address of a real person, s-mail, e-mail)
#Passphrase (Min 6, Alpha and Nums)

[Note: e-mail must work, s-mail *may* be checked.]

<i>Agio Fee Schedule</i>

The Agio Fee is the e-gold system equivalent of an account maintenance fee.  It is deducted in monthly installments, calculated based on average daily balance since last assessed. 1% per annum.

<i>Spend Fee Schedule</i>

Spend Fees are the e-gold system equivalent of  transaction fees.  They are deducted from Recipient account upon receipt of Spend.

:Au: max (5g) ~$20
:Ag: max (250g) ~$15

- - -

The long explanation (from them)-

1. Account Name

Specify a name for your account. The account name will be displayed when someone is spending or receiving e-metal to this account. An optional description may be entered.
:Examples: "Joe's e-gold account", "ABC Widgets Inc", "Caesar T. Oglethorpe".

2. User Name

Specify a user name for yourself. The user name will be displayed in the account history, to clarify one account user from another. Currently a single user is supported per account. You may also enter a description of the user if desired.
:Example User Names: "Joe Hampton", "Dr. N.", "Caesar T. Oglethorpe".
:Example Descriptions: "Trustee", "Deputy Comptroller"

3. Point of Contact

Specify the account point of contact information. This must be the name and address of a real person. Please fill in a complete mailing address.

4. Passphrase

New e-gold Account Passphrase: (Minimum length 6) (Must contain Alphabetical and Numerical characters) (Do not reuse a passphrase from other web sites) New e-gold Account Passphrase again: (Verify)

5. Turing Number Entry

NOTE: This is not your e-gold account number.
Your new account number will be emailed to you.


- - -

<b>Gold Now - http://www.goldnow.st</b>


Two services at the moment:

#Buy emoney with your credit card: A service charge of 15% will be added to all orders.
#Sell or Exchange your emoney here: 2%

Order  your debit card here: Not.
Fund your debit card using emoney or cash here: Not.
Fund your debit card using your credit card coming soon: Maybe.
Access your debit card account here. Not.


- - -

<b>1MDC - https://www.1mdc.com/</b>


If you love e-gold, Pecunix, <nowiki>GoldMoney</nowiki>, e-bullion®, you'll love 1mdcGrams.

No storage fees, no spend fees! - Amazing privacy!

1mdc->1mdc: no charge

<i>Open account:</i>

#Your e-gold account:
#Your initials: (lower case letters only, max 5)
#Choose a 1mdc password: (8-16 chars & a mix of upper & lower case and digits.
#Choose a 1mdc PIN:
#Your email: (Must function)

It is incredibly easy to sell your 1mdcGrams and get a cheque or wire.
:icegold.com    cambist.net    spacegold.com    e-fidex.com
and others already have automated spend pages for you to sell your 1mdcGrams. So easy.
open2exchange features superb interface to 1mdc!

- - -

